Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.30,0:00:13.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, you're saying you can't tell us, no matter what?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.41,0:00:20.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You see, there's this alien—
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.67,0:00:20.58,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Scieszka, keep quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.46,0:00:23.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, you couldn't have wound up in the power distribution station
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.50,0:00:25.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,just because you'd \Nlost your way, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.56,0:00:27.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What exactly were you \Ndoing in there?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.49,0:00:28.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sergeant...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.47,0:00:32.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you \Ngoing to do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.23,0:00:44.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, Lieutenant Ross...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.06,0:00:50.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's something going on \Nwithin the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.20,0:00:51.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something very dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.69,0:00:55.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.17,0:01:03.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry-san, \Nwhat do we do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.39,0:01:05.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going back to \NResembool for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.67,0:01:09.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'd like to talk to Ed and Al, \Nbut I don't know where they are.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.63,0:01:11.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then what should I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.45,0:01:14.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about? You're coming with me!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.81,0:01:16.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But what about \Nmy books at home?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.68,0:01:18.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Leave them there.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.80,0:01:42.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.56,0:01:45.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can take this off now, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.05,0:01:47.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Be my guest.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.92,0:01:52.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, that's better.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.35,0:01:54.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Crimson...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.51,0:01:59.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, well, if it isn't the Flame Major—make that Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.17,0:02:01.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is something the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.22,0:02:03.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Archer!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.71,0:02:06.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is the meaning of this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.02,0:02:10.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you have some issue with the Crimson Alchemist, Lt. Colonel Zolf J. Kimbly?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.98,0:02:12.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.15,0:02:17.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Lt. Colonel was imprisoned on false charges,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.10,0:02:21.32,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,and just before he was subjected to unlawful human experimentation at the 5th Laboratory,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.32,0:02:23.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he made a successful escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.13,0:02:28.89,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Thanks to the Lt. Colonel's testimony, the facts about the 5th Laboratory are coming to light.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.87,0:02:32.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,False charges?! \NThat's outrageous!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.77,0:02:37.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do not forget that \Nfor this operation,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.51,0:02:40.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Führer has granted me \Nthe rank of colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.56,0:02:46.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By the way, who was \Nthat telephone call from?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.79,0:02:48.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.13,0:02:50.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know of \Na town called Liore?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.68,0:03:00.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.93,0:03:15.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.66,0:03:20.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.94,0:03:25.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.68,0:03:31.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.73,0:05:20.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, you're the one...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.21,0:05:24.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. I killed Greed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.37,0:05:27.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! What good \Ndoes it do to say that now?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.38,0:05:30.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel, I don't know \Nwhat you were thinking,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.99,0:05:35.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but to me, you and Greed were both criminals who kidnapped my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.64,0:05:38.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's more, \Nhe also killed Dante-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.17,0:05:42.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.76,0:05:48.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look out!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.16,0:05:54.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A snake?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.25,0:06:00.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not who I'm after.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.49,0:06:05.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Greed-san chose death \Nrather than being sealed up again.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.95,0:06:08.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was, more than anything, \Na proud man.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.39,0:06:12.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so, I believe he wanted to be defeated by you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.07,0:06:18.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The ones who I detest are \Nthe military who killed my friends,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.46,0:06:20.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and those two \Nwho dress all in black,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.77,0:06:23.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,as well as the man \Nwho betrayed my friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.07,0:06:25.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kimbly!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.32,0:06:36.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why don't you eat it? \NThey're nutritious.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.69,0:06:39.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why don't {\i1}you{\i0} eat it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.46,0:06:43.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, my. If I did that, it would be cannibalism, wouldn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.87,0:06:53.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're getting close to Liore, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.78,0:06:55.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.21,0:06:58.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder how Rose-san is doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.99,0:07:00.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.57,0:07:02.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't pretend you've forgotten.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.40,0:07:04.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, you've been a little worried about her, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.40,0:07:07.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, Martel, how soon \Nbefore we get to Ishbal?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.05,0:07:08.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.18,0:07:11.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've long since entered Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.94,0:07:25.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is Ishbal?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.22,0:07:27.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's nothing here, \Nhuh, Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.54,0:07:31.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We need some way \Nto find Scar, but this...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.63,0:07:33.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What exactly are you \Nlooking for, anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.82,0:07:40.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.61,0:07:42.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was a man who said
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.49,0:07:45.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they had created a Philosopher's Stone before Ishbal was destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.82,0:07:48.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That can't be true.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.77,0:07:50.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They offered no resistance
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.39,0:07:52.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and were killed before they \Nhad a chance to take up arms.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.91,0:07:54.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No way they offered \Nno resistance!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.82,0:07:59.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The military and Ishbal had \Na long and tense military relationship.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.30,0:08:02.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then an incident where a soldier mistakenly shot a civilian took place,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.21,0:08:05.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the Ishbalans rose up.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.71,0:08:09.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's really \Nhow it was presented...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.42,0:08:12.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I didn't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.82,0:08:15.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was in that laboratory for a little over fourteen years.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.25,0:08:19.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Since just after the civil war in Ishbal broke out?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.80,0:08:22.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks to being turned into a Chimera, \NI may look young,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.17,0:08:24.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I'm your fairly older sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.05,0:08:25.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean aunt—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.24,0:08:27.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.92,0:08:32.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were a special operations unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.23,0:08:48.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We weren't told \Nwhat our destination was
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.55,0:08:52.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,or what the details of our mission were \Nuntil the last minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.48,0:08:55.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the way \Nthey usually did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.93,0:09:00.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.78,0:09:11.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're in dire straits!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.03,0:09:12.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.76,0:09:16.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know! But people are being killed!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.76,0:09:17.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The mission we had been given \Nwas to infiltrate the Ishbalan city
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.01,0:09:19.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and conduct large-scale subversive activities.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.01,0:09:19.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In any case, let's get someplace safe!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.22,0:09:23.77,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,It was under the pretext of preventing them \Nfrom carrying out acts of terrorism
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.77,0:09:26.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that they were planning to commit against Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.02,0:09:53.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And you're saying that's what \Nbrought about the Ishbalan uprising?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.66,0:09:56.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What reason would the military have for starting a war with Ishbal?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.78,0:09:58.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know \Nwhat the reason was.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.58,0:09:59.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There, you see?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.02,0:10:02.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I do have proof.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.92,0:10:11.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.39,0:10:14.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just listen to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.86,0:10:19.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right after the Ishbalan \NCivil War started,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.47,0:10:21.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we were placed in custody.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.35,0:10:24.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Anyone who resisted...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.60,0:10:25.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.85,0:10:29.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on here?! \NWe were following military orders!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.94,0:10:43.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who survived were \Ntaken to the 5th Laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.12,0:10:51.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dolcetto!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.88,0:10:53.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.50,0:11:02.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.83,0:11:03.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.48,0:11:26.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They made you a Chimera.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.37,0:11:31.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The military tried to \Ncompletely silence us. Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.91,0:11:34.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because you knew a secret that \Nabsolutely could not be leaked out—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.98,0:11:36.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the truth about \Nthe start of the war.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.05,0:11:38.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But why?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.61,0:11:40.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why would the military \Nprovoke Ishbal?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.05,0:11:45.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone's there?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.05,0:11:45.36,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.36,0:11:46.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a lead!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.77,0:11:49.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not getting away!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.55,0:12:05.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now then, let's have you tell me \Nwhat you're doing here.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.34,0:12:09.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Th-This area is \Noff-limits to civilians.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.31,0:12:13.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're here to check on the security of the old Ishbalan cities.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.70,0:12:17.49,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Then you could've just shown yourselves instead of sneaking around, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.49,0:12:22.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. He may not look it, \Nbut my brother is a State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.92,0:12:26.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you guys, moles?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.64,0:12:30.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, could those men be...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.78,0:12:39.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yo...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.86,0:12:41.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.25,0:12:43.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then the Colonel is here too?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.22,0:13:01.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well aren't you a familiar face?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.05,0:13:03.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah, same old shrimp who's so small
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.94,0:13:05.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you'd lose sight of him \Namong the grains of san—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.90,0:13:06.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you calling that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.39,0:13:12.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hear you've been raising hell \Nall over the place.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.27,0:13:16.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Southern Command Center, \Nas well as the Ishbalan escort train.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.63,0:13:23.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Anyhow, you're under \Nmy command from now on.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.03,0:13:25.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a moment, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.23,0:13:28.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're lucky that Havoc caught you when they were out scouting.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.57,0:13:33.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But we're supposed to have permission to continue our journey independently.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.04,0:13:37.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, once called up, \NI become a dog of the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.46,0:13:38.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.79,0:13:43.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They've come all the way out to this \Nremote region in a military transport train.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.59,0:13:49.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't tell me there's a war.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.04,0:13:53.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're just quelling \Na somewhat seditious area.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.38,0:13:57.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our target is a town about two \Nkilometers south-southeast of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.19,0:13:59.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're pretty heavily armed, considering.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.80,0:14:01.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.67,0:14:03.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shall I tell you why you're here?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.40,0:14:05.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's Scar, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.26,0:14:09.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were just looking \Nfor him ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.55,0:14:16.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are your reasons \Nfor pursuing Scar?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.87,0:14:21.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we don't put him down, \Nhe's going to make a lot of trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.38,0:14:25.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, Alphonse-kun,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.17,0:14:27.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you don't have to force yourself to pretend you're eating.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.52,0:14:29.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, you're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.64,0:14:32.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll kill that woman!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.73,0:14:37.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.83,0:14:41.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The latest photographs \Nfrom our surveillance balloon.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.41,0:14:48.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.13,0:14:50.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It couldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.37,0:14:53.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A transmutation circle \Nmade from the whole city?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.42,0:15:07.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who would do such a thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.48,0:15:07.33,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,I won!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.33,0:15:08.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scar.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.42,0:15:10.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So it {\i1}is{\i0} him?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.72,0:15:13.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-kun, do you know what his objective is?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.18,0:15:18.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No. So, what town is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.32,0:15:19.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The town is named Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.92,0:15:24.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Last year, its tyrannical priest retired,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.38,0:15:26.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and peace has just barely returned with the stationing of troops there.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.85,0:15:28.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sergeant Fuery...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.98,0:15:28.49,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.49,0:15:30.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He knows.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.27,0:15:34.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Liore, you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.47,0:15:36.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An armed uprising in Liore?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.96,0:15:38.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This shouldn't be happening!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.63,0:15:40.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We put down that bogus priest and brought peace to the city!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.96,0:15:42.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.20,0:15:45.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After that, the people divided into \Na priest faction and a citizen's faction,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.59,0:15:47.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and there has been \Nterrible confusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.12,0:15:49.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When the military went in \Nto gather a situation report,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.26,0:15:51.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,both factions stood against them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.66,0:15:54.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why didn't you \Ntell me about this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.63,0:15:56.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was involved in this \Nfrom the start!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.18,0:15:59.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard the report from Hughes, but I kept it back.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.64,0:16:00.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.29,0:16:02.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because it was too much for you to handle.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.28,0:16:18.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't Ed-kun and Al-kun know about Brigadier General Hughes?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.62,0:16:20.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Apparently not.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.72,0:16:24.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If he tells them now, they'd probably just dash back to Central, and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.68,0:16:27.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He is an important military asset, \Nand everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.02,0:16:32.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-kun and his brother are in a dangerous position right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.38,0:16:38.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He probably wants to have them in a place where he can keep his eye on them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.84,0:16:45.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, is my brother here?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.98,0:16:52.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You will give me first priority when reporting.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.15,0:16:56.75,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,And if you will observe my earlier conditions, \NI will grant you permission.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.66,0:16:59.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed! What are you doing here?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.25,0:17:03.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At his insistence,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.65,0:17:06.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am having him \Nreconnoiter the town of Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.99,0:17:10.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're sending one of our precious State Alchemists out to sightsee?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.50,0:17:14.26,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Which is exactly why no matter what happens, \Nhe will come back to us alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.26,0:17:15.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.75,0:17:18.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he knows more about Liore than anyone else does.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.48,0:17:22.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please put your mind at ease.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.47,0:17:25.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said he would \Nleave his brother here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.37,0:17:31.61,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,He's not about to leave his dear brother here and disappear by himself on us, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.92,0:17:36.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why didn't you tell me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.05,0:17:37.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I had, would you have given me permission?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.74,0:17:41.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've learned about Liore, and now you're confused.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.37,0:17:46.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why I'm going to \Ncool my head now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.13,0:17:56.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Phew, it was hot in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.63,0:18:01.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Be careful. The way the military sees it, you're a wanted person.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.32,0:18:04.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, are you serious about this? You're going to Liore alone?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.40,0:18:10.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Leaving you behind \Nwas the bargaining point.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.07,0:18:13.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Archer doesn't trust us at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.38,0:18:17.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if that transmutation circle is for a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.60,0:18:19.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If it is, I'm going to destroy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.33,0:18:23.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel, behave yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.32,0:18:28.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know. I held myself back in front of \Nthat Archer guy earlier, didn't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.74,0:18:31.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to kill those guys in black and Kimbly first.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.51,0:18:34.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Taking my revenge against \Nthe military comes after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.09,0:18:36.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not going to let you \Ndo that, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.32,0:18:45.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, be really careful, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.81,0:18:46.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.02,0:18:53.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,M-Major...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.60,0:18:55.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're here?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.52,0:19:01.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel Archer said to \Nleave your silver watch here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.93,0:19:05.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh yeah. I guess it would be trouble if someone found out my position.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.93,0:19:15.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward Elric, \Nwhy did you come here?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.95,0:19:19.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fate, maybe?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.55,0:19:21.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.30,0:19:24.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I doubt you two \Neven believe in fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.21,0:19:38.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A new silver watch has arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.79,0:19:46.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give this one the transmutation amplification treatment as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.97,0:20:12.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.13,0:20:15.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You were driven out of the city because of that priest, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.56,0:20:19.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That Cornello guy was \Npositively awful, all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.86,0:20:24.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By the way, I get the feeling that \NI've seen your face around somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.16,0:20:26.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.73,0:20:28.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Must be one of those \Ncommon faces.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.30,0:20:32.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the Holy Mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.50,0:20:37.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're in luck!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.17,0:20:37.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.50,0:20:40.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the Holy Mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.45,0:21:01.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Rose?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.88,0:21:06.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please go back inside!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.82,0:21:10.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Colonel said that under no circumstances was anyone to see you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.00,0:21:12.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because I'm officially deceased?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.22,0:21:15.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At least allow me to do as I like \Nin the evening.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.08,0:21:16.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.29,0:21:17.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You sure are pesky.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.21,0:21:24.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.30,0:21:28.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kimbly!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.32,0:21:30.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.88,0:21:38.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To think that we would be \Nseeing the boy here again...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.74,0:21:42.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What should we do, Gluttony?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.02,0:21:46.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pride told us, right? \NThe Ishbal...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.23,0:21:48.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,um...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.15,0:21:51.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kill anyone who knows the truth about Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.64,0:21:52.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's too bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.29,0:21:57.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I smell it. I smell it!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.32,0:22:02.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The smell of the Ishbalan beast!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.42,0:23:40.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.08,0:23:42.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 40: "The Scar"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.72,0:23:47.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Some people say that the scars \Non your body disappear in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.45,0:23:51.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But there are some scars that you can't get rid of.
